
        Naval Gunnery Ballistics
        
A set decimal places to 10
A write numbers with decimal point

N108 0                  . Set to 1 to print integration steps
N155 −1                 . Drag / no drag: 1 for just drag, −1 for both

    The following specifications are those of the British
    BL 15 inch Mark I gun, used on capital ships from 1915
    until 1959.
      https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/BL_15_inch_Mk_I_naval_gun

    Properties of the gun

N100 15.0               . Calibre in inches
N101 30.0               . Muzzle elevation in degrees

    Properties of the projectile
    
N102 1938.0             . Projectile mass (m) in pounds
N103 2458.0             . Muzzle velocity, ft/sec
N104 0.25               . Coefficient of drag (C_d) (dimensionless)

    Properties of the Earth and atmosphere
    
N105 32.174             . Acceleration of gravity (g), ft/sec²
N106 0.0765             . Atmospheric density (ISA) (ρ), lb/ft³
N109 1373003.7          . Energy of one pound of TNT in foot lbf

    Calculation parameters
    
N107 2.0                . Time step (s), seconds

    Constants
    
N110 3.1415926535897932 . π
N111 180.0              . Degrees in π radians
N112 2.0                . Constant 2.0
N113 12.0               . Inches per foot
N114 0                  . Constant 0
N115 3.0                . Feet per yard
N116 0.5                . Constant 0.5
N117 1                  . Constant 1
N118 0.05               . Constant 0.05 to round to one decimal place
N119 1000000000.0       . Constant to scale from computational to display

    Derived quantities
    
 N120                   . Muzzle elevation in radians
 N121                   . Projectile frontal area (a), ft²
 
    Working storage
    
 N130 – N131            . Calculation temporaries
 
 N140                   . v (instantaneous velocity)
 N141                   . θ (instaneous angle)
 N142                   . v_x (x component of velocity)
 N143                   . v_y (y component of velocity)
 N144                   . x (instantaneous range)
 N145                   . y (instantaneous altitude)
 N146                   . d (instantaneous drag)
 N147                   . p (instantaneous momentum)
 N148                   . v_d (drag-adjusted velocity)
 N149                   . x_y (range in yards)
 N150                   . y_y (altitude in yards)
 N151                   . t (current time)
 N152                   . x_l (last x printed/plotted)
 N153                   . y_l (last y printed/plotted)
 N154                   . t_l (last time printed)
 N156                   . y_max (maximum altitude)
 
    Curve Drawing parameters
    
N160 1000000000000000   . Scale factor from computation to plot
                        . Because the Curve Drawing Apparatus has
                        . axes of ± (length 2), the following scale
                        . factors are half the maximum value to be
                        . plotted.
N161 27000.00           . X axis scale factor (xscale)
N162 14000.00           . Y axis scale factor (yscale)
N163 1.0                . Constant 1.0


